.TH MKPASS-GUI 1 "October 2026" "mkpass 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mkpass-gui \- Qt graphical interface for mkpass password generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkpass-gui
[\fIQT_OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkpass-gui
is the graphical Qt user interface for the
.B mkpass
stateless password and passphrase generator.
.PP
It provides an intuitive visual interface to regenerate strong passwords on-demand using a \fBMaster Password\fR and a \fBService Name\fR.
.PP
Key Features of the GUI:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBReal-time Service Autocomplete\fR: Instant suggestions derived from the local SQLite database.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInteractive Controls\fR: Dynamic form controls for algorithm selection (Argon2, SHA512, Diceware, WordNet pattern), length adjustments, character set toggles, and service comments.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDatabase Management Dialog\fR: Built-in manager accessible via the Database menu to view, search, inspect full record details, edit comments, and delete saved service configurations.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPreferences & Settings Dialog\fR: Configure persistent default generation parameters, default algorithm, and automatic update checking behavior.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIntegrated Self-Updating System\fR: Non-intrusive background update checks and on-demand check via \fBHelp \-> Check for Updates...\fR. Includes cryptographic SHA-512 integrity verification and direct installer execution.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBClipboard Security\fR: Instant clipboard copy button with automatic clipboard wiping upon application shutdown.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBIntegrated Help Manual\fR: Comprehensive user manual accessible directly from the Help menu.

.SH OPTIONS
.B mkpass-gui
accepts standard Qt command-line options:
.TP
\fB\-style\fR \fISTYLE\fR
Specify the Qt GUI style (e.g., fusion, breeze, cleanlooks).
.TP
\fB\-geometry\fR \fIGEOMETRY\fR
Set the main window size and position.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display standard command-line help options.

.SH USE CASES
.TP
.B Standard Desktop Password Generation
1. Launch \fBmkpass-gui\fR.
2. Type your Master Password in the password field.
3. Type or select a Service Name (e.g. "github.com").
4. Adjust options if required (algorithm, length, character sets, optional comment).
5. Click \fBGenerate\fR or press Enter.
6. Click \fBCopy to Clipboard\fR.
.TP
.B Managing Stored Service Configurations
1. Open the \fBDatabase\fR menu and select \fBManagement\fR.
2. Search or browse saved service entries.
3. Double-click an entry or click Details to view its full configuration record.
4. Select and delete obsolete service configurations.
.TP
.B Checking for Software Updates
1. Open the \fBHelp\fR menu and click \fBCheck for Updates...\fR.
2. If a new version is available, review the release notes in the update dialog.
3. Click \fBDownload and Install\fR to automatically download the verified package and perform the update.
.TP
.B Configuring Application Defaults
1. Open the \fBEdit\fR menu and select \fBSettings\fR (or \fBPreferences\fR).
2. Adjust default algorithm, length, character sets, or toggle periodic update checking.
3. Click \fBSave\fR to write settings to \fBmkpass.conf\fR.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkpass/config.db
SQLite database storing local non-secret service configuration entries, comments, and options history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mkpass/mkpass.conf
TOML user configuration file containing persistent defaults and update preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mkpass/update_state.json
Local cache storing update check timestamps, HTTP ETags, and latest known release information.

.SH SEE ALSO
